[FINAL-TEXT] **This is the root cause.** dswb1's br0.99 has **two IP addresses**: `10.0.0.18/28` (correct) **and** `10.0.0.17/32` (a keepalived VIP that shouldn't be there in /32 form). FRR selects the /32 mask when building its OSPF Hello packets on that interface. dswb2 receives those Hellos and rejects them — the log shows the error every 10 seconds (every Hello interval):

